WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.820
so let's look at a problem
regarding isotopic abundance and atomic

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:16.830
mass. the question says the abundances of
the following silicon isotopes are as

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:25.140
follows: silicon 28 is ninety two point
two three percent, silicon 29 is four

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:32.099
point six seven percent, and silicon 30
is 3.10% so that means out of all the

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:36.690
silicon atoms in the universe ninety two
point two three percent of them weigh

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.620
twenty-eight atomic mass units, four
point six seven percent of them weigh

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.989
twenty nine atomic mass units, and three
point one zero percent of them weigh

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:52.410
thirty atomic mass units. so the question
is what is the average atomic mass of

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:58.710
silicon. so if this is confusing go and
check out my tutorial on nuclides

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:04.680
symbols, we want to understand atomic
mass we want to understand atomic number

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:10.140
and mass number and we want to
understand what isotopes are, so if you

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:15.340
are unclear go ahead and check out that
tutorial first, if everything makes sense give this a shot.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.020
so here are the
relevant values, now what are we going to

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.960
do with them? as it turns out to get the
average atomic mass all we need to do is

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:46.649
multiply the mass number of each isotope
by its abundance, so let's do that now.

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:52.979
first we have silicon 28 so let's put 28
times zero point nine two two three

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:59.939
that is 92 point two three percent of
one, or a whole. to that we will add 29

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:05.700
for the mass number of silicon 29 and
multiply that by zero point zero four

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:11.370
six seven, that is four point six seven
percent of one or a whole, which

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:17.260
represents the atomic mass
of silicon. and lastly we have 30 for the

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:22.450
mass number of silicon 30 and we will
multiply that by zero point zero three

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:28.150
one zero, which is three point one zero
percent of one. and now all we need to do

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:34.180
is add these up. let's also be clear that
our answer should have three sig figs

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:40.030
because these values in the parentheses
have four sig figs, three sig figs, and

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:45.090
three sig figs respectively, so that will
limit our answer to three sig figs. and

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:51.100
if we plug all of that into a calculator
we do get 28 point one and that is the

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:56.500
average atomic mass of silicon that we
would find on the periodic table. so that

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:01.510
means if we took a sample of silicon
atoms and added all of their masses

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.680
together and then divided by the number
of atoms there are, we would get twenty

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:11.240
eight point one atomic mass units as the
average mass of all of those silicon atoms.

